RSA SecurID is an offline token that is designed to create authentication codes. At fixed intervals, a built in clock and a seed. This seed is unique to the token, and is encoded
  into the token at the factory. This seed is also loaded into the RSA SecurID server. To authenticate a user, they must enter their PIN, and the number displayed on the
  token at that moment. In an offline environment, to authenticate the user, the system must know the seeds, of which the system will calculate what code the token should
  have generated. If they match, the user is authenticated. 
  Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RSA_SecurID
